            <ArticleTitle>Draft Genome Sequence of Bacillus sp. FMQ74, a Dairy-Contaminating Isolate from Raw Milk.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">e01512-16</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1128/genomeA.01512-16</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Representatives of the genus Bacillus are common milk contaminants that cause spoilage and flavor alterations of dairy products. Bacillus sp. FMQ74 was isolated from raw milk on a Danish dairy farm. To elucidate the genomic basis of this strain's survival in the dairy industry, a high-quality draft genome was produced.</AbstractText>
